WEBVTT

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:01.358
from readers on the feedback boards
on the Times website,

00:03:01.382 --> 00:03:03.274
from users saying,

00:03:03.298 --> 00:03:05.712
""Me too, and here's my tale of woe."

00:03:05.736 --> 00:03:08.122
I call it "software rage."

00:03:08.146 --> 00:03:09.345
And man, let me tell you,

00:03:09.369 --> 00:03:13.792
whoever figures out how to make money
off of this frustration will --

00:03:13.816 --> 00:03:16.097
Oh, how did that
get up there? Just kidding.

00:03:16.121 --> 00:03:17.269
(Laughter)

00:03:17.293 --> 00:03:20.172
Ok, so why is the problem accelerating?

00:03:20.196 --> 00:03:22.161
And part of the problem is, ironically,

00:03:22.185 --> 00:03:24.280
because the industry
has put so much thought

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.257
into making things easier to use.

00:03:26.281 --> 00:03:27.882
I'll show you what I mean.

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:32.341
This is what the computer
interface used to look like, DOS.